{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1044","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Deduction Queries"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is an array $$$a$$$ of $$$2^{30}$$$ integers, indexed from $$$0$$$ to $$$2^{30}-1$$$. Initially, you know that $$$0 \\leq a_i \\lt 2^{30}$$$ ($$$0 \\leq i \\lt 2^{30}$$$), but you do not know any of the values. Your task is to process queries of two types:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 l r x"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":": You are informed that the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise xor"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the subarray $$$[l, r]$$$ (ends inclusive) is equal to $$$x$$$. That is, $$$a_l \\oplus a_{l+1} \\oplus \\ldots \\oplus a_{r-1} \\oplus a_r = x$$$, where $$$\\oplus$$$ is the bitwise xor operator. In some cases, the received update contradicts past updates. In this case, you should "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ignore"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the contradicting update (the current update)."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 l r"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":": You are asked to output the bitwise xor of the subarray $$$[l, r]$$$ (ends inclusive). If it is still impossible to know this value, considering all past updates, then output "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$-1$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that the queries are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"encoded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". That is, you need to write an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"online"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" solution."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$q$$$ ($$$1 \\leq q \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the number of queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next $$$q$$$ lines describes a query. It contains one integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 2$$$) — the type of query."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The given queries will be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"encoded"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the following way: let $$$last$$$ be the answer to the last query of the second type that you have answered (initially, $$$last = 0$$$). If the last answer was $$$-1$$$, set $$$last = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If $$$t = 1$$$, three integers follow, $$$l'$$$, $$$r'$$$, and $$$x'$$$ ($$$0 \\leq l', r', x' \\lt 2^{30}$$$), meaning that you got an update. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First, do the following"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$l = l' \\oplus last$$$, $$$r = r' \\oplus last$$$, $$$x = x' \\oplus last$$$ "}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and, if $$$l \\gt r$$$, swap $$$l$$$ and $$$r$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This means you got an update that the bitwise xor of the subarray $$$[l, r]$$$ is equal to $$$x$$$ (notice that you need to ignore updates that contradict previous updates)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If $$$t = 2$$$, two integers follow, $$$l'$$$ and $$$r'$$$ ($$$0 \\leq l', r' \\lt 2^{30}$$$), meaning that you got a query. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First, do the following"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":":"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$l = l' \\oplus last$$$, $$$r = r' \\oplus last$$$ "}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and, if $$$l \\gt r$$$, swap $$$l$$$ and $$$r$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For the given query, you need to print the bitwise xor of the subarray $$$[l, r]$$$. If it is impossible to know, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$-1$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Don't forget to change the value of $$$last$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed there will be at least one query of the second type."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After every query of the second type, output the bitwise xor of the given subarray or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$-1$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if it is still impossible to know."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12\n2 1 2\n2 1 1073741822\n1 0 3 4\n2 0 0\n2 3 3\n2 0 3\n1 6 7 3\n2 4 4\n1 0 2 1\n2 0 0\n2 4 4\n2 0 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n-1\n-1\n-1\n5\n-1\n6\n3\n5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n1 5 5 9\n1 6 6 5\n1 6 5 10\n2 6 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"12\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, the real queries (without being encoded) are:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"12"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 1 2"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 0 1073741823"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 1 2 5"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 1 1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 2 2"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 1 2"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 2 3 6"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 1 1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 1 3 0"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 1 1"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 2 2"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2 3 3"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The answers for the first two queries are $$$-1$$$ because we don't have any such information on the array initially. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The first update tells us $$$a_1 \\oplus a_2 = 5$$$. Note that we still can't be certain about the values $$$a_1$$$ or $$$a_2$$$ independently (for example, it could be that $$$a_1 = 1, a_2 = 4$$$, and also $$$a_1 = 3, a_2 = 6$$$). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" After we receive all three updates, we have enough information to deduce $$$a_1, a_2, a_3$$$ independently. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, notice that after the first two updates we already know that $$$a_5 \\oplus a_6 = 12$$$, so the third update is contradicting, and we ignore it."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1044D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1044/problem/D"}